  play system-details/ubuntu2604 -------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Play mode: hardn's System Details screen$
# (pkg/screens/systemdetails), inferred from origin/main$
# (unreleased), read from a simulated host by the real reader$
# (pkg/engine/details). It only reads: no plan, no y/N, no$
# journal. Nothing on this machine changes: every command and$
# file is the fake's.$
$
# Info: system-details/ubuntu2604$
# web-01.example.net runs Ubuntu 26.04, as the VM of 2026-10-21$
# (vmtest.md §8.5): kernel 7.0.0-38-generic, sudo-rs 0.2.13.$
# lslogins is in util-linux-extra there, and answers as on$
# Debian 13 (vm-runs/s1/02-login.log).$
$
# System Details ###############################################$
$
  OS and Kernel ------------------------------------------------$
$
   -  OS                   Ubuntu 26.04 (Resolute)$
   -  Kernel               7.0.0-38-generic$
   -  Uptime               3 days, 5 hours, 12 minutes$
$
  Host and IPs -------------------------------------------------$
$
   -  Hostname             web-01$
   -  eth0                 192.0.2.20/24$
$
  Users --------------------------------------------------------$
$
   -  alice                sudo$
$
  CPU and Load -------------------------------------------------$
$
   -  Model                QEMU Virtual CPU version 2.5+$
   -  CPUs                 4, 1 socket$
   -  Load (1, 5, 15 min)  0.12, 0.08, 0.03$
$
  Disk ---------------------------------------------------------$
$
   -  /                    /dev/vda1 ext4$
   -  Used                 4.2 of 38.6 GiB (11%)$
$
  Memory -------------------------------------------------------$
$
   -  Used                 1.2 of 3.8 GiB (30%)$
$
  Last Login ---------------------------------------------------$
$
   -  root                 None recorded$
   -  alice                Oct 20 11:42 from 192.0.2.10$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Refresh              Read the host again$
$
   0) Return$
$
    > Enter selection [0-1 or q]: 0$
$
  simulated system ---------------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Nothing was applied.$
$

